{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מארת", :translit "m'orot", :gloss "lights"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling: מארת lacks the vav of מאורת, indicating the moon's light was diminished."}], :frame {:text "The word מארת is written without a vav (unlike its form in Genesis 1:16), signaling that one of the two lights was diminished. The Talmud explains that the moon complained to God that two kings cannot share one crown, so God told it to diminish itself (Chullin 60b). Shabbat 156a warns that those born under the sun's influence may be predisposed to sun-worship; providing a second luminary mitigates idolatrous veneration of the sun as sole sovereign of the sky.", :sources ["Chullin 60b" "Shabbat 156a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling: מארת lacks the vav of מאורת, indicating the moon's light was diminished.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:03:39.065928886Z", :model "glm-5.2"}